.TH SDL_GetProcessOutput 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetProcessOutput \- Get the
.BR SDL_IOStream
associated with process standard output.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_process.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_IOStream * SDL_GetProcessOutput(SDL_Process *process);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The process must have been created with
.BR SDL_CreateProcess ()
and pipe_stdio set to true, or with
.BR SDL_CreateProcessWithProperties ()
and
.BR SDL_PROP_PROCESS_CREATE_STDOUT_NUMBER
set to
.BR SDL_PROCESS_STDIO_APP \[char46]
.PP
Reading from this stream can return 0 with
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
returning
.BR SDL_IO_STATUS_NOT_READY
if no output is available yet\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I process
The process to get the output stream for\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the output stream or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CreateProcess (3),
.BR SDL_CreateProcessWithProperties (3),
.BR SDL_GetProcessInput (3)
